{"id":"torres-del-paine-w","title":"Torres del Paine: the W Trek","who":"Classic route · Patagonia on foot","when":"October to April (refugios open mid-September to mid-April)","vehicle":"On foot, 4–5 days, refugios or campsites","kind":"walk","color":"#1e40af","summary":"About 80 km in the shape of a W through Chile's most famous park: the granite towers at dawn, the French Valley between hanging glaciers, and the blue icebergs of Grey Glacier. Fierce winds; no wild camping, so book the refugios months ahead.","sources":[{"label":"Global Summit Guide: W Trek complete guide (January 2025 trip)","url":"https://globalsummitguide.com/w-trek-torres-del-paine-complete-guide/"},{"label":"RMI Guides: Torres del Paine dispatch (February 2025)","url":"https://www.rmiguides.com/blog/expedition/torres_020125/desc"}],"approximate":"The usual east-to-west W; the line follows the park's trails where they were found.","km":74,"bbox":[-73.1815,-51.0724,-72.8661,-50.9423],"stops":[{"name":"Refugio Central","place":"Refugio Central, Torres del Paine","at":[-50.9656,-72.866],"text":"The east end, by the Hotel Las Torres.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ce/Torres_del_Paine_y_cuernos_del_Paine%2C_montaje.jpg/500px-Torres_del_Paine_y_cuernos_del_Paine%2C_montaje.jpg","page":"Torres del Paine National Park","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Torres_del_Paine_y_cuernos_del_Paine%2C_montaje.jpg","credit":"Karen Chan 16 y Miguel.v ( local | logs | global ) (originales), y Jorge Morales Piderit (montaje).","license":"CC BY 4.0"}},{"name":"Refugio Chileno","place":"Refugio Chileno","at":[-50.9572,-72.9106],"text":"Up the Ascencio valley; sleep here to reach the towers at dawn.","source":{"label":"Global Summit Guide (2025)","url":"https://globalsummitguide.com/w-trek-torres-del-paine-complete-guide/"},"photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/92/Torres_del_Paine%2C_Chile_by_Karen_Chan_16.jpg/500px-Torres_del_Pa